      "title": "START HERE - KREA 2 ENTITY REFERENCE SHEETS",
      "properties": {
        "aux_id": "pixaroma/ComfyUI-Pixaroma",
        "ver": "72516552d286901accf5a10fe9619c89b6784932",
        "Node name for S&R": "PixaromaNote",
        "cnr_id": "ComfyUI-Pixaroma",
        "ue_properties": {
          "widget_ue_connectable": {},
          "version": "7.8",
          "input_ue_unconnectable": {}
        }
      },
      "widgets_values": [
        "{\"version\":1,\"content\":\"<h1>Krea 2 Entity Reference Sheets - Ref2VA Ready</h1><p><b>Edit only the first two panels.</b> In panel 1, describe three or four reusable scene entities. A subject can be a person, animal, creature, vehicle, building, prop, landscape feature, food item, or anything else. Turn off an unused row. Panel 2 applies one shared visual treatment to every row and understands Pixaroma tags.</p><ol><li>Leave the node in <b>Queue</b> mode and click Run once.</li><li>Krea 2 generates one nine-view identity sheet for every enabled row.</li><li>Human and humanoid sheets include front, three-quarter and profile face views; front, three-quarter and profile full-body views; front and rear T-poses; and one identity-detail view.</li><li>Non-humanoid subjects automatically substitute equivalent close-ups, orthographic views, elevations or plan views.</li><li>Load the resulting PNGs into Ref2VA as ref_image_0, ref_image_1, and so on, then define them as &lt;Subject 1&gt; from &lt;Picture 1&gt;, &lt;Subject 2&gt; from &lt;Picture 2&gt;, etc.</li></ol><p>All nine panels must depict the same single identity, not nine different characters.</p>\",\"buttonColor\":\"#f66744\",\"lineColor\":\"#f66744\",\"width\":4340,\"height\":320,\"backgroundColor\":\"#2a2a2a\"}",
        ""
      ],
      "widgets_values_named": {
        "note_json": "{\"version\":1,\"content\":\"<h1>Krea 2 Entity Reference Sheets - Ref2VA Ready</h1><p><b>Edit only the first two panels.</b> In panel 1, describe three or four reusable scene entities. A subject can be a person, animal, creature, vehicle, building, prop, landscape feature, food item, or anything else. Turn off an unused row. Panel 2 applies one shared visual treatment to every row and understands Pixaroma tags.</p><ol><li>Leave the node in <b>Queue</b> mode and click Run once.</li><li>Krea 2 generates one nine-view identity sheet for every enabled row.</li><li>Human and humanoid sheets include front, three-quarter and profile face views; front, three-quarter and profile full-body views; front and rear T-poses; and one identity-detail view.</li><li>Non-humanoid subjects automatically substitute equivalent close-ups, orthographic views, elevations or plan views.</li><li>Load the resulting PNGs into Ref2VA as ref_image_0, ref_image_1, and so on, then define them as &lt;Subject 1&gt; from &lt;Picture 1&gt;, &lt;Subject 2&gt; from &lt;Picture 2&gt;, etc.</li></ol><p>All nine panels must depict the same single identity, not nine different characters.</p>\",\"buttonColor\":\"#f66744\",\"lineColor\":\"#f66744\",\"width\":4340,\"height\":320,\"backgroundColor\":\"#2a2a2a\"}",
        "note_dom": ""
